            <ArticleTitle>[Mega-dosages vitamin D: progressive medicine?].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1959-61</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Although the risk of vitamin intoxication is well recognised, massive doses of these preparations continue to be prescribed, especially in the so-called 'alternative' medical sector. We describe a patient with hypervitaminosis D due to administration of megadoses of vitamin D in the absence of an obvious indication. Mode of action and symptoms of vitamin D intoxication are discussed. It is emphasized that vitamin preparations should only be used when strictly indicated and that close clinical and biochemical supervision is necessary.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
